  "query_preview": "../ Friday to Tuesday / At the mid and higher level  \nsteering levels of the atmosphere the upper level trough which was\nin the gulf travels east in British Columbia by Friday morning, \nas a building mid level ridge builds and moves east over the gulf.\nThe ridge axis should shift east of the panhandle by early \nSunday. A weakening closed low over Bering Sea moves east to be \nnorth of the Pribilof Islands and stalling by Sunday as well. A \ntrough about this low will rotate south over the Aleutians and \ninto the North Pacific, then to the western gulf Mon-Tue time \nframe depending on the model solution following. \n\nSo what does this mean weather wise for Southeast... showers from\nthe midweek into Thursday, tapering off/ending as improvements \nFriday - early Saturday period due to the ridge moving through and\nclearing weather out. Models beginning to come to agreement of \nfairly organized from to push through the eastern gulf Sunday to \nMonday. Gusty winds for the coastline Sunday, and then likely\nshowers to start the upcoming week. The very long forecast\nis showing hints that will be need to watched closely to see how\nthat situation develops.  \n\nTemperature-wise at or just below normal values, with higher \nelevations of the Klondike and the higher Canadian Haines Highways\nto possible see snow or snow rain mix for the weekend period.",
